---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Research Exhibition">

<section class="hero">

  <div class="hero-content">

    <h1>Living World from Different Perspectives</h1>

    <p>
      Exploring biodiversity through the eyes of researchers.
    </p>

  </div>

</section>

<main>


<section class="intro">

<h1>About the Exhibition</h1>

<p>
<strong>Living World from Different Perspectives</strong> is a public
photography exhibition that I organized to showcase research conducted within the
Ecology and Genetics Research Unit at the University of Oulu.
The exhibition offers visitors an opportunity to explore the organisms
we study, the methods we use, and the scientific questions that drive
our research.
</p>

<p>
Each photograph captures a study system through the perspective of the
researcher. Together they reveal the remarkable diversity of life and
highlight how ecological and evolutionary research contributes to our
understanding of the natural world.
</p>

</section>

<!-- Why -->

<section class="feature">

<img
src="/images/exhibition-overview.webp"
alt="Research exhibition"
/>

<div>

<h2>Research Through Our Eyes</h2>

<p>
Have you ever wondered how researchers see their study organisms?
How do we find them, observe them, and understand their ecology?
This exhibition invites visitors to experience the natural world from
the perspective of scientists working on wildlife, biodiversity,
genetics, and evolution.
</p>

<p>
Each exhibit combines photography with concise explanations of the
research focus, the study species, and the motivation behind each
project.
</p>

</div>

</section>

<!-- QR -->

<section class="feature reverse">

<img
src="/images/exhibition-overview2.webp"
alt="QR code exhibition"
/>

<div>

<h2>Explore Further</h2>

<p>
Every photograph is accompanied by a QR code linking to additional
information about the project. Visitors can continue exploring each
study system, learn about the featured species, and discover the
research behind every image.
</p>

</div>

</section>

<!-- Gallery -->

<section class="gallery">

<h2>Gallery</h2>

<p class="section-intro">
Photographs featured in the exhibition.
</p>

<div class="gallery-grid">

<img src="/images/exhibition-1.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition2.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition3.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition-4.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition5.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition6.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition7.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition-8.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition9.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition10.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition-11.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition12.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition13.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">
<img src="/images/exhibition14.webp" alt="" class="gallery-image">

</div>

</section>

<!-- Exhibition -->

<section class="impact">

<h2>The Exhibition</h2>

<p>
The exhibition consists of fourteen large-format photographs presenting
different study systems investigated by members of the Ecology and
Genetics Research Unit. The first appearance of the exhibition was 
during the Researchers' Night at the University of Oulu in 2023. The l
exhibition can be periodically visited at the Botanical gradientsof the 
University of Oulu. Beneath every image, visitors find a concise
description of the research topic together with a QR code leading to
more detailed information online.
</p>

</section>

<!-- Credits -->

<section class="credits">

<h2>Project</h2>


<p>
The project was funded by <a href="https://www.oulu.fi/en/research/biodiverse-arctic-and-global-resilience/biodiverse-anthropocenes"
target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> Biodiverse Anthropocenes Research Programme
</a> at the University of Oulu, and presented during the Researchers' Night
2023.
</p>

<div class="credits-grid">

<div>

<h3>Aim</h3>

<p>
To showcase the research at the Ecology and Genetics 
Research Unit, University of Oulu
</p>

</div>

<div>

<h3>Photography</h3>

<p>
Images contributed by researchers of the Ecology and Genetics
Research Unit, and rights belong to the researchers.
</p>

</div>

</div>

</section>


<div id="lightbox" class="lightbox">
  <button id="prev" class="arrow">&#10094;</button>

  <img id="lightbox-img" src="" alt="">

  <button id="next" class="arrow">&#10095;</button>
</div>

</main>

</Layout>

<style>

.hero{
min-height:55vh;
display:flex;
align-items:center;
padding:4rem max(2rem, calc((100vw - 1300px)/2));
background:
linear-gradient(rgba(0,0,0,.35),rgba(0,0,0,.35)),
url("/images/exhibition-hero.webp");
background-size:cover;
background-position:center;
color:white;
}

.hero-content{
max-width:700px;
}

.hero h1{
font-size:4rem;
margin-bottom:1rem;
}

.hero p{
font-size:1.3rem;
line-height:1.6;
}

main{
max-width:1100px;
margin:0 auto;
padding:4rem 2rem;
}

p{
  line-height:1.8;
  font-size:1.05rem;
}
section{
margin-bottom:3rem;
}

.intro,
.impact{
max-width:800px;
margin:0 auto 5rem;
}

.feature{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
gap:4rem;
align-items:center;
}

.feature.reverse img{
order:2;
}

.feature.reverse div{
order:1;
}

.feature img{
width:100%;
border-radius:18px;
}

.gallery{
max-width:1100px;
margin:0 auto 5rem;
}

.gallery h2,
.gallery .section-intro{
max-width:800px;
margin-left:auto;
margin-right:auto;
text-align:left;
}

.gallery-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
}

.gallery-grid img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
}

.credits{
max-width:900px;
margin:auto;
}

.credits-grid{
display:grid;
grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;
gap:3rem;
margin-top:2rem;
}

@media(max-width:900px){

.feature{
grid-template-columns:1fr;
}

.feature.reverse img,
.feature.reverse div{
order:initial;
}

.gallery-grid{
grid-template-columns:1fr;
}

.credits-grid{
grid-template-columns:1fr;
}

.hero h1{
font-size:3rem;
}

}


.lightbox{
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.9);
  display: none;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  z-index: 1000;
}

.lightbox.active{
  display: flex;
}

.lightbox img{
  max-width: 90%;
  max-height: 90%;
  object-fit: contain;
}

.gallery-image{
  cursor: pointer;
}

.arrow{
  position:absolute;
  top:50%;
  transform:translateY(-50%);
  background:none;
  border:none;
  color:white;
  font-size:3rem;
  cursor:pointer;
  padding:1rem;
}

#prev{
  left:2rem;
}

#next{
  right:2rem;
}

.arrow:hover{
  opacity:0.7;
}
</style>



<script>
const images = document.querySelectorAll(".gallery-image");
const lightbox = document.getElementById("lightbox");
const lightboxImg = document.getElementById("lightbox-img");

const prev = document.getElementById("prev");
const next = document.getElementById("next");

let current = 0;

function showImage(index){
  current = index;
  lightboxImg.src = images[current].src;
}

images.forEach((img, index) => {
  img.addEventListener("click", () => {
    lightbox.classList.add("active");
    showImage(index);
  });
});

next.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
  e.stopPropagation();
  showImage((current + 1) % images.length);
});

prev.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
  e.stopPropagation();
  showImage((current - 1 + images.length) % images.length);
});

lightbox.addEventListener("click", () => {
  lightbox.classList.remove("active");
});
</script>